1053,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1053 Arabic Hadees: 1057
1054,"On the authority of ʿUwaym ibn Sāʿidah, who narrated that the Prophet (peace be upon him) came to them in the Mosque of Qubāʾ and said: ""Indeed, Allah — Blessed and Exalted — has praised you well regarding purification in the matter of your mosque. What is this purification with which you purify yourselves?"" They said: ""By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, we know of nothing except that we had neighbors from the Jews, and they used to wash their posteriors after defecation, so we washed as they washed.""Narrated by Aḥmad and al-Ṭabarānī in the three [Muʿjams], and its chain includes Shuraḥbīl ibn Saʿd. Mālik, Ibn Maʿīn, and Abū Zurʿah weakened him, while Ibn Ḥibbān authenticated him."
1055,"On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: When this verse was revealed: ""In it are men who love to purify themselves"" [At-Tawbah: 108], the Prophet (peace be upon him) sent to Uwaym ibn Sa'idah and said: ""What is this purification with which Allah has praised you?"" They said: O Messenger of Allah, no man or woman among us goes out to relieve themselves except they wash their private parts, or he said: their anus. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""It is this."" Narrated by Al-Tabarani in Al-Kabir, and its chain is good, except that Ibn Ishaq is a mudallis (one who practices tadlis), and he has narrated it with 'an'anah (ambiguous narration)."
1056,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1056 Arabic Hadees: 1071
1057,"On the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam, from his father, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah came to the mosque which was founded on piety, the Mosque of Quba. He stood at its door and said: 'Indeed Allah has praised you excellently regarding purification. What is your purification?' We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we are People of the Book, and we find that cleansing with water (istinja) is incumbent upon us, and we do it today.' He said: 'Indeed Allah - Mighty and Majestic - has praised you excellently regarding purification,' then he recited: {In it are men who love to purify themselves, and Allah loves those who purify themselves} [At-Tawbah: 108].""Al-Tabarani narrated it in Al-Mu'jam Al-Kabir, and in its chain is Shahr ibn Hawshab, about whom they differed, but Ahmad, Ibn Ma'in, Abu Zur'ah, and Ya'qub ibn Shaybah authenticated him."
1058,"Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Salam said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) came to us—meaning Quba—and said: 'Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has praised you regarding purification in the best terms; will you not inform me?' He meant His saying: {In it are men who love to purify themselves, and Allah loves the purifiers} [At-Tawbah: 108]. They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we find it written upon us in the Torah'—meaning purification with water.""Narrated by Ahmad from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, and he did not say: ""from his father,"" as Al-Tabarani said; and Shahr is also in its chain."
