1082,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1082 Arabic Hadees: 690
1083,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1083 Arabic Hadees: 1115
1084,"Anas ibn Malik said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) went out to a land in Medina called Buthan. He said: 'O Anas, pour water for me for ablution.' So I poured for him. When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) finished his need, he came to the vessel, and a cat had come and lapped from the vessel. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) stood waiting for it until the cat drank, then he performed ablution. I mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) the matter of the cat, so he said: 'O Anas, the cat is from the household furnishings; it will not defile anything nor make it impure.'""Narrated by al-Tabarani in al-Saghir, and in its chain is Umar ibn Hafs al-Makki; Ibn Hibban authenticated him, al-Dhahabi said: ""It is not known who he is."""
1085,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1085 Arabic Hadees: 1129
1086,"And from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father: that water for ablution was placed for him, and a cat drank from it, so he proceeded to perform ablution from it. They said: 'O Abu Qatadah, the cat has drunk from it!' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: ""The cat is from the people of the house, and indeed it is among those who go around you [men] and those who go around you [women].""'Narrated by Ahmad - and it is in the Sunan except for his saying: 'The cat is from the people of the house' - and it is from the narration of Abdullah from his father, and its narrators are trustworthy, except that it contains Al-Hajjaj ibn Arta'ah, and he is trustworthy but a mudallis (one who practices tadlis).And a hadith about the cat and the dog will follow."
1087,"On the authority of Al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) called me for water. I went to a tent and found in it a Bedouin woman. I said: ""This is the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and he wants water to perform ablution. Do you have any water?"" She said: ""May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah! By Allah, there is no soul under the heaven nor carried by the earth more beloved to me than his soul, nor more honored. But this water skin is made from the skin of a dead animal (not slaughtered), and I do not wish to impurity the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) with it."" So I returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and informed him. He said: ""Go back to her, for if she has tanned it, then its tanning purifies it."" So I returned to her and mentioned that to her. She said: ""Yes, by Allah, I have tanned it."" So I brought him water from it.Narrated by Ahmad and Al-Tabarani in Al-Mu'jam Al-Kabir with part of it. In its chain is Ali ibn Yazid from Al-Qasim, and there is discussion about both of them, but they have been deemed trustworthy."
