1121,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1121 Arabic Hadees: 876
1122,"Al-Abbas said: They would enter upon the Prophet (peace be upon him) without using the tooth-stick (siwak), so he said: ""You enter upon me with foul mouths and do not use the tooth-stick. Were it not that I would impose hardship on my Ummah, I would have enjoined the tooth-stick upon them just as I enjoined ablution upon them."" And Aisha said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) continued to mention the tooth-stick until we feared that a Quranic verse would be revealed concerning it. Narrated by Abu Ya'la, Al-Bazzar, and Al-Tabarani in Al-Kabir; among its narrators is Abu Ali Al-Sayqal, who is unknown (majhul). I say: Many hadiths concerning the tooth-stick and what relates to it in prayer will follow, Allah willing."
1123,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1123 Arabic Hadees: 911
1124,"On the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, who said: Abu Umamah narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Any man who performs ablution intending to pray, then washes his hands, every sin from his hands falls away with the first drop. Then when he rinses his mouth and sniffs water into his nose and blows it out, every sin from his tongue and lips falls away with the first drop. Then when he washes his face, every sin from his hearing and sight falls away with the first drop. Then when he washes his hands up to the elbows and his feet up to the ankles, he becomes free from every sin as on the day his mother gave birth to him."" He said: ""Then if he stands for prayer, Allah raises his rank, and if he sits, he sits sinless.""Narrated by Ahmad and al-Tabarani in al-Kabir and al-Awsat. In the chain of Ahmad is Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram from Shahr, and there is disagreement about citing them as evidence, but the correct view is that they are both trustworthy, and the criticism of them does not harm their reliability."
1125,"On the authority of Abu Muslim, who said: I entered upon Abu Umamah while he was sitting in the mosque and burying lice in the gravel. I said: ""O Abu Umamah, a man narrated to me from you that you said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: 'Whoever performs ablution and perfects it—washing his hands and face, wiping over his head and ears—then stands for the obligatory prayer, Allah will forgive him on that day whatever his two feet walked to, whatever his two hands grasped, whatever his two ears heard, whatever his two eyes saw, and whatever his soul whispered of evil.'"" He said: ""By Allah, I have heard it from the Prophet of Allah (peace be upon him) more times than I can count.""Narrated by Ahmad and al-Tabarani similarly in al-Kabir. In its chain is Abu Muslim, and I did not find anyone who authenticated him or criticized him, except that al-Hakim mentioned him in al-Kuna and said: Abu Hazim narrated from him. And here Aban ibn Abdullah narrated from him. And similarly Ibn Abi Hatim mentioned him."
1126,"And from Abu Ghalib that he met Abu Umamah in Homs and asked him about things, and he narrated to them that he heard the Prophet - peace be upon him - saying: ""There is no Muslim servant who hears the call to prayer and then stands for his ablution - except that he is forgiven with the first drop that reaches his hand from that water, and by the number of those drops, until he finishes his ablution - except that his past sins are forgiven, and he stands for his prayer and it is supererogatory."" Abu Ghalib said: I said to Abu Umamah: ""Did you hear this from the Prophet - peace be upon him?"" He said: ""Yes, by the One Who sent him with the truth as a bearer of glad tidings and a warner, not once, nor twice, nor three times, nor four, nor five, nor six, nor seven, nor eight, nor nine, nor ten and ten,"" and he clapped his hands. Narrated by Ahmad and al-Tabarani in al-Kabir."
1127,"And he has in *al-Ṣaghīr* from him also, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""When a Muslim performs ablution and washes his hands, the sins committed by his hands fall away; then when he washes his face, the sins looked upon by his eyes fall away; then when he wipes his head, the sins heard by his ears fall away; then when he washes his feet, the sins walked toward by his feet fall away; then he stands for prayer, and that is a supererogatory merit.""And Abū Ghālib is disagreed upon regarding citing him as evidence, and the rest of its narrators are trustworthy; and al-Tirmidhī has graded Abū Ghālib as *ḥasan* and also authenticated him.And Aḥmad narrated it via a sound chain, and added that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Ablution expiates what came before it, then the prayer becomes supererogatory."" And he also narrated it via a sound chain, and added: ""When he performs ablution as he was commanded."""
1128,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1128 Arabic Hadees: 1022
1129,"On the authority of Abu Umamah, in a hadith he traced back to the Prophet - may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him - he said: ""There is no Muslim who performs ablution, washing his hands, rinsing his mouth, and performing ablution as commanded - except that Allah removes from him the sins he committed that day with his tongue, what his hands touched, and where his feet walked, until sins fall away from his limbs. Then when he walks to the mosque, one step records a good deed and another erases a sin.""Al-Tabarani narrated it in Al-Mu'jam Al-Kabir, and in its chain is Laqit Abu Al-Mushawir, who narrated from Abu Umamah, and Al-Jariri and Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated from him. Ibn Hibban mentioned him in Al-Thiqat (The Trustworthy Narrators) and said: He makes mistakes and is contradicted (in narration)."
1130,"On the authority of Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When a Muslim performs ablution, sin departs from his hearing, his sight, his hands, and his feet."" He said: Then Abu Taybah came while we were being narrated this, and he said: ""What are you being narrated?"" So we mentioned to him what we had been narrated. A man said: ""I heard Amr ibn Abasah narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and he added to it."" He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""There is no Muslim who spends the night in a state of purity, then wakes up during the night, remembers Allah, and asks Allah for good from the good of this world and the Hereafter, except that Allah grants it to him."" Narrated by Ahmad and al-Tabarani in al-Mu'jam al-Kabir and al-Awsat with similar wording, and he said in it: ""Whoever spends the night pure while remembering Allah,"" and its chain is good (hasan). I say: The hadith of Ibn Umar concerning one who spends the night in a state of purity will come after this."
1131,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1131 Arabic Hadees: 1116
1132,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1132 Arabic Hadees: 1120
1133,"On the authority of Uthman ibn Affan, that he called for water, then rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nose, then washed his face three times, and his forearms three times, and wiped his head and the tops of his feet, then he laughed and said to his companions: ""Will you not ask me what made me laugh?"" They said: ""What made you laugh, O Commander of the Faithful?"" He said: ""I saw the Messenger of Allah - peace be upon him - perform ablution as I performed ablution, then he laughed and said: 'Will you not ask me what made me laugh?' They said: 'What made you laugh, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Verily, when a servant calls for ablution and washes his face, Allah removes from him every sin he committed with his face; then when he washes his forearms, it is likewise; (and if he wipes his head, it is likewise); and when he purifies his feet, it is likewise.'""I said: It is in the Sahih in abbreviated form, and it was narrated by Ahmad and Abu Ya'la, and its narrators are trustworthy."
1134,"On the authority of Thalabah ibn 'Abbad, from his father, who said: I do not know how many times the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) narrated it to him, in pairs and individually. He said: There is no servant who performs ablution, perfecting the ablution, washing his face until water flows over his chin, then washing his arms until water flows over his elbows, then washing his feet until water flows from his ankles, then stands and prays — except that Allah forgives him his previous sins.Al-Tabarani narrated it in Al-Kabir, and he narrated it with another chain, saying: On the authority of Thalabah ibn 'Imarah, and he said: Thus did Ishaq al-Dabari narrate it from 'Abd al-Razzaq. And he erred in his name, and the correct one is Thalabah ibn 'Abbad. And its narrators are trustworthy."
1135,"And on the authority of Abu Ushanah al-Ma'afiri that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir saying: ""I do not say today upon the Messenger of Allah - may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him - what he did not say. I heard the Messenger of Allah - may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him - saying: 'Two men from my Ummah, one of them gets up at night, striving to purify himself while he has knots upon him, so he performs ablution; when he washes his hand a knot is untied, when he washes his face a knot is untied, when he wipes his head a knot is untied, when he washes his feet a knot is untied. Then the Lord - Mighty and Majestic - says to those behind the veil: Look at this servant of Mine striving for himself; whatever My servant asks of Me, it is his.'""Ahmad and al-Tabarani in al-Kabir narrated it, and he added in it: ""I heard the Prophet - may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him - saying: 'Whoever says upon me what I did not say, let him take his seat in Hellfire.'"" And he added: ""'Men from my Ummah, one of them gets up at night'"" then he mentioned it. And it has two chains of narration with them, the men of one of them are trustworthy."
1136,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1136 Arabic Hadees: 166
1137,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1137 Arabic Hadees: 304
1138,"On the authority of Anas, from the Prophet — may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him — he said: ""The likeness of my Ummah is like a river from which one bathes five times a day; what filth could remain on him? He proceeds to perform ablution and washes his hands, and every sin his hands touched falls away. Then he rinses his mouth, and every sin his tongue spoke falls away. Then he washes his face, and every sin his eyes looked at falls away. Then he wipes his head, and every sin his ears heard falls away. Then he washes his feet, and every sin his feet walked to falls away."" Narrated by Abu Ya'la, and in its chain is Mubarak ibn Suhaym, and they have unanimously agreed upon his weakness."
1139,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1139 Arabic Hadees: 344
1140,"On the authority of Abu al-Darda', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""I am the first to be permitted to prostrate on the Day of Resurrection, and I am the first to raise my head. I will look before me and recognize my Ummah among the nations. Behind me will be the like of that, on my right the like of that, and on my left the like of that."" A man said: ""How do you recognize your Ummah, O Messenger of Allah, from among the nations from Noah to your Ummah?"" He said: ""They are bright-faced and white-limbed from the traces of ablution; no one else has that except them. And I recognize them because they will be given their records in their right hands, and I recognize them because their offspring will run before them.""Narrated by Ahmad and al-Tabarani in al-Kabir in abbreviated form, and in its chain is Ibn Lahi'ah, who is weak. It has another chain that will be mentioned in the chapter on the Resurrection."
1141,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1141 Arabic Hadees: 438
1142,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1142 Arabic Hadees: 480
1143,"On the authority of Uqbah ibn Amir, who said: I came with twelve riders until we alighted at the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). My companions said: ""Who will tend to our camels while we go and learn from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and when he finishes, we will learn from him what we heard?"" I said: ""I will."" Then I said to myself: ""Perhaps I am losing out; will my companions hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) what I did not hear?"" So I attended one day and heard a man saying: The Prophet of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs a complete ablution, then stands for prayer, his sins will be as on the day his mother gave birth to him."" Narrated by Al-Tabarani in Al-Awsat, and it is in its entirety in the Book of Faith, mentioned earlier, and the discussion on it has preceded."
1144,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1144 Arabic Hadees: 504
1145,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""There is no Muslim who performs ablution for prayer, then rinses his mouth, except that every sin he spoke with his tongue comes out with the drops of water. And he does not sniff water into his nose except that every sin he smelled with his nose comes out with the drops of water. And he does not wash his face except that every sin he looked at with his eyes falls away from his eyes with the drops of water. And he does not wash any part of his hands except that every sin he struck with them comes out with the drops of water. And he does not wash any part of his feet except that every sin he walked to with them comes out with the drops of water. Then when he goes out to the mosque, a good deed is recorded for him with every step he takes, and a sin is erased from him thereby, until he reaches his place of standing (in prayer)."" Narrated by Al-Tabarani in Al-Awsat, and it is in the Sahih in abbreviated form, and its narrators are trustworthy."
1146,"On the authority of Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: ""Whoever spends the night in a state of purity, an angel spends the night in his garment (or close to him). He does not wake up at any hour of the night except that the angel says: 'O Allah, forgive Your servant, for he spent the night in a state of purity.'""Al-Bazzār and Al-Ṭabarānī in *Al-Muʿjam Al-Kabīr* reported it. In its chain is Maymūn ibn Zayd; Al-Dhahabī said: Abū Ḥātim deemed him weak. And in Al-Ṭabarānī's chain is Al-ʿAbbās ibn ʿUtbah; Al-Dhahabī said: He narrates from ʿAṭāʾ, and he transmitted this hadith, and said: ""His hadith is not authentic."" I (the author) say: Sulaymān Al-Aḥwal reported it from ʿAṭāʾ, and he is among the men of *Al-Ṣaḥīḥ*; likewise it is with Al-Bazzār, and I hope its chain is *ḥasan*. And the hadith of ʿAmr ibn ʿAbasah concerning whoever spends the night in a state of purity has preceded in the chapter before this one. Al-Ṭabarānī's wording is: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Purify these bodies, may Allah purify you; for there is no servant who spends the night in a state of purity except that an angel spends the night with him in his garment. He does not turn over at any hour of the night except that he says: 'O Allah, forgive Your servant, for he spent the night in a state of purity.'"""
1147,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1147 Arabic Hadees: 854
1148,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1148 Arabic Hadees: 1092
1149,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1149 Arabic Hadees: 131
1150,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1150 Arabic Hadees: 491
1151,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1151 Arabic Hadees: 548
1152,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1152 Arabic Hadees: 684
1153,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1153 Arabic Hadees: 569
1154,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1154 Arabic Hadees: 731
1155,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1155 Arabic Hadees: 844
1156,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1156 Arabic Hadees: 142
1157,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1157 Arabic Hadees: 192
1158,"On the authority of Rabah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Huwaytib, from his grandmother, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: ""Whoever does not believe in me has not believed in Allah, and whoever does not love the Ansar has not believed in me, and there is no prayer for one who has no ablution, and there is no ablution for one who does not mention the name of Allah upon it.""Ahmad narrated it from her directly, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and he narrated it from her on the authority of her father. And Allah knows best. In it is Abu Thifal; Al-Bukhari said: There is a weakness in his hadith. And the rest of its narrators are narrators of the Sahih."
1159,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1159 Arabic Hadees: 201
1160,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1160 Arabic Hadees: 280
1161,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1161 Arabic Hadees: 281
1162,"On the authority of Abu al-Nadr: ""Uthman called for water for ablution while al-Zubayr, Talhah, Ali, and Sa'd were with him. He performed ablution while they watched. He washed his face three times, then poured water over his right hand three times, and over his left hand three times. He wiped his head, then sprinkled water on his right foot three times, then washed it. Then he sprinkled water on his left foot, then washed it three times. Then he said to those present: 'I adjure you by Allah - Mighty and Majestic - do you know that the Messenger of Allah - peace be upon him - used to perform ablution just as I have done now?' They said: 'Yes.'"" And that was due to something that had reached him.Narrated by Abu Ya'la. And Abu al-Nadr did not hear from any of the Ten [Companions promised Paradise], and in it also is Ghassan ibn al-Rabi'; al-Daraqutni weakened him once, and said another time: 'Sound (salih),' and Ibn Hibban mentioned him in al-Thiqat (the trustworthy narrators)."
1163,"On the authority of Humran ibn Aban, who said: ""I saw Uthman ibn Affan call for water for ablution while he was at the door of the mosque. He washed his hands, then rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nose, then washed his face three times, then washed his hands up to the elbows three times, then wiped his head and passed his hands over the outside of his ears, then passed them over his beard, then washed his feet up to the ankles three times. Then he stood and prayed two rak'ahs, then said: 'I performed ablution for you as I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) perform ablution, then I prayed two rak'ahs as I saw him pray.' He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said when he finished his two rak'ahs: 'Whoever performs ablution as I have performed ablution, then prays two rak'ahs in which he does not let his mind wander, will be forgiven what is between them and his prayer of yesterday.'""I said: Ahmad narrated it, and it is in the Sahih in abbreviated form, and its narrators are trustworthy."
1164,"On the authority of ʿUthmān, he called for water for ablution, rinsed his mouth, sniffed water into his nose, washed his face three times, washed his forearms three times, wiped his head, and washed his feet. Then he laughed and said: ""Will you not ask me what made me laugh?"" We said: ""What made you laugh, O Commander of the Faithful?"" He said: ""I laughed because the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) called for water for ablution near this place, and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) performed ablution just as I did, then he laughed just as I laughed, then he said: 'Will you not ask me what made me laugh?' We said: 'What made you laugh, O Prophet of Allah?' He said: 'What made me laugh is that when a servant performs ablution and washes his face, Allah removes from him every sin he committed with his face; then when he washes his forearms, it is likewise; then when he wipes his head, it is likewise; then when he washes his feet, it is likewise.'""Narrated by Al-Bazzār, and its narrators are narrators of the Ṣaḥīḥ, and it is in the Ṣaḥīḥ in an abbreviated form."
1165,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1165 Arabic Hadees: 581
1166,"On the authority of Yazid ibn al-Bara' ibn 'Azib — and he was a governor in Oman, and he was like the best of governors — he said: My father said: ""Gather together so that I may show you how the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to perform ablution and how he used to pray; for I do not know how long my companionship with you will last."" He said: So he gathered his sons and his family, and called for water for ablution. He rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nose, washed his face three times, washed his right hand three times, washed this (the left) three times — meaning the left — then wiped his head and his ears, both their outer and inner parts, washed this foot — meaning the right — three times, washed this foot — meaning the left — three times, then said: ""This is how (it is done); I have not fallen short in showing you how the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to perform ablution.""Narrated by Ahmad, and its narrators are trustworthy."
1167,"From ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn (Abī) Qurād, who said: ""I went out with the Prophet ﷺ for Ḥajj. He said: I saw him go out to relieve himself, so I followed him with a water vessel or a cup. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he wanted to answer the call of nature, would go far away. So I sat waiting for him by the road until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned. Then I said to him: 'O Messenger of Allah, the ablution (wuḍūʾ).' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me, poured water on his hand and washed it, then put his hand into the vessel and poured it out, then poured water on his hand once, then wiped his head, then took water in his hand once, then scooped water with his hand and struck it on the backs of his feet, sprinkling with his hand on the backs of his feet.""I said: This is how it appears in the original text.Narrated by Aḥmad — and al-Nasāʾī and Ibn Mājah narrated from it: ""When he wanted to relieve himself, he would go far away"" — and its narrators are trustworthy."
1168,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1168 Arabic Hadees: 674
1169,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1169 Arabic Hadees: 711
1170,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1170 Arabic Hadees: 823
1171,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1171 Arabic Hadees: 940
1172,"And from Rashid Abu Muhammad al-Himmani, who said: ""I saw Anas ibn Malik at the corner (al-zawiyah), so I said to him: 'Inform me about the ablution (wudu) of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), how was it? For it has reached me that you used to pour water for his ablution.' He said: 'Yes.' Then he called for ablution water, and a basin and a cup were brought to him—the cup was carved (he says) just as it was carved (in his land)—and it was placed before him. He poured water over his hands from the vessel, washing his palms thoroughly. Then he rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water into his nose three times, and washed his face three times. Then he brought out his right hand and washed it three times, then washed the left three times. Then he wiped his head once, except that he passed his wet hands over his ears, wiping them. Then he put both his hands together into the water."" He said: ""Then he mentioned the rest of the hadith.""Narrated by al-Tabarani in al-Awsat, and its chain of transmission is good (hasan)."
1173,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1173 Arabic Hadees: 1020
1174,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1174 Arabic Hadees: 1058
1175,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1175 Arabic Hadees: 1140
1176,"On the authority of Ibn Abbas: ""A Bedouin came to the Prophet — may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him — and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, how is ablution?' So the Messenger of Allah — may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him — called for water for ablution, washed his right hand three times, then put his right hand into the vessel, then rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nose three times, washed his face and hands three times, wiped his head and the outer parts of his ears along with his head, then washed his feet three times, then said: 'This is how ablution is; whoever adds to it has transgressed and done wrong.'""Al-Tabarani narrated it in Al-Mu'jam Al-Kabir, and he has another hadith in the Sahih other than this one. In its chain is Suwaid ibn Abd al-Aziz; Ahmad and Yahya and a group weakened him, and Duhaym authenticated him."
1177,"On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: ""I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) while he was performing ablution, and before him was a vessel the size of a mudd, and if it increased, it increased only slightly, and if it decreased, it decreased only slightly. So he washed his hands, rinsed his mouth, and sniffed water into his nose three times each. He washed his face three times, ran his fingers through his beard, washed his forearms three times, wiped his head and ears twice each, and washed his feet until he cleaned them thoroughly. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, is this the ablution?' He said: 'This is how my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me.'""Al-Tabarani narrated it in Al-Awsat, and in its chain is Nafi' Abu Hormuz, and he is very weak."
1178,"On the authority of Wā'il ibn Ḥajar, who said: ""I was present with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when a vessel containing water was brought to him. He poured water over his right hand three times, then dipped his right hand into the vessel and poured water over his left hand three times. Then he dipped his right hand again, took a handful of water, rinsed his mouth, sniffed water into his nose, and blew it out three times. Then he put both hands into the vessel, took up water with them, and washed his face three times. Then he ran his fingers through his beard, wiped the inside of his ears, and inserted his little fingers into his ears so that the water would reach inside. Then he wiped his neck and the inside of his beard with the remaining water from washing his face. Then he washed his right forearm three times until he passed the elbow, and washed the left one likewise until he passed the elbow. Then he wiped his head three times, wiped the outside of his ears, and wiped his neck and the inside of his beard with the remaining water from wiping his head. Then he washed his right foot three times, ran his fingers between his toes, passed water over the ankle, and raised the water up the shin. Then he did the same with the left foot. Then he took a handful of water with his right hand, placed it on his head until it trickled down the sides of his head, and said: 'This is the completion of wuḍū'.' Then he entered his prayer niche, lined up the people behind him, and looked to his right and to his left.""I said: So he narrated the ḥadīth.It was narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr and by al-Bazzār. In its chain is Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār; al-Nasā'ī said: ""He is not strong."" Ibn Ḥibbān mentioned him in al-Thiqāt. In the chain of al-Bazzār and al-Ṭabarānī is Muḥammad ibn Ḥajar, and he is weak. In the ḥadīth of al-Bazzār there is additional length concerning the matter of the prayer, which will come in the description of the prayer, Allah willing."
1179,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1179 Arabic Hadees: 903
1180,"On the authority of Abu Bakrah, he said: ""I saw the Messenger of Allah - peace be upon him - perform ablution. He washed his hands three times, rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water into his nose three times, washed his face three times and his forearms up to the elbows, wiped his head moving his hands from the front to the back, and from the back to the front, then washed his feet three times, and ran his fingers through his toes and through his beard.""Al-Bazzar narrated it and said: ""It is not narrated from Abu Bakrah except through this chain of narration, and Bakkar is not problematic, and his son Abd al-Rahman is trustworthy."" I say: Al-Bazzar's shaykh, Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Awwam, I did not find anyone who wrote his biography, and the rest of its narrators are narrators of the Sahih."
1181,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1181 Arabic Hadees: 292
1182,"On the authority of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbbās ibn Yaḥyā ibn Khallād al-Zuraqī, who said: ""We entered upon ʿAbd Allāh ibn Unays, and he said: 'Shall I not show you how the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) performed ablution and how he prayed?' We said: 'Yes.' So he washed his hands three times each, wiped his head forward and backward, wiped his ears, and washed his feet three times each. Then he took a garment, wrapped himself in it, and prayed. He said: 'Thus did I see my beloved, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), perform ablution and pray.'""Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Awsaṭ, and in its chain is ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbbās ibn Yaḥyā ibn Khallād al-Zuraqī, for whom I found no biographical entry."
1183,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1183 Arabic Hadees: 656
1184,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 1184 Arabic Hadees: 678
1185,"On the authority of Abu Kahil, who said: ""I passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) while he was performing ablution. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Allah has given us much good through you.' So he washed his hands three times, then rinsed his mouth three times, and sniffed water into his nose three times, and washed his face three times, and his forearms three times, and wiped his head without specifying a number, and washed his feet without specifying a number. And he said: 'O (Abu) Kahil, place the purifying water in its proper places, and leave the remainder of your purifying water for your family; do not make your family thirsty, and do not overburden your servant.'"" Al-Tabarani narrated it in Al-Mu'jam Al-Kabir, and in its chain is Al-Haytham ibn Jammaz, and he is matruk (abandoned/weak narrator)."
