1197,"On the authority of ʿUmar ibn Abān ibn Mufaḍḍal al-Madanī, who said: Anas ibn Mālik showed me the ablution (wuḍūʾ). He took a water vessel (rikwah) and placed it on his left side, then poured water on his right hand and washed it three times. Then he turned the vessel with his right hand and washed it three times, then wiped his head three times, and took fresh water for his ear canals and wiped them. I said: ""You have wiped your ears!"" He said: ""O boy, they are part of the head, not part of the face."" Then he said: ""O boy, did you see? And did you understand? (Or shall I repeat it for you? I said: It sufficed me and I understood.)"" He said: ""Thus did I see the Messenger of Allah — peace be upon him — perform ablution.""Al-Ṭabarānī narrated it in Al-Awsaṭ and Al-Ṣaghīr. Al-Dhahabī said: ""And ʿUmar ibn Abān is not known who he is."" I (the author) say: Ibn Ḥibbān mentioned him in Al-Thiqāt (the trustworthy narrators)."
